+## Actual parent and closing behavior
+
+The proposed placement is grounded in the real ordinary path: `GameEngine.TurnLifecycle.cs:1484–1504` encloses Stage, agent waiting snapshot, terminal wait and Finalize in one participating callback. Browser preparation/idle/expected-G-finalization instead spans separate phases at1507–1554, so this ordinary wrapper is not accepted browser lifetime coverage. The source also has direct callers in MainMenu1493/2267, explorer-produced action1384, normal action1398, in-place service turn1447 followed by refresh1454, and existing decline recursion2357. MainMenu1493 is inside an already-started participating operation; explorer changes and selected-action consumption can precede this new root entry. The design expressly refuses to retroactively enroll them or reacquire an exclusive root lane from an actual nested parent. Their enclosing owner integration remains open. Existing recursion is descriptive source evidence, not permission for F1 replay: FD/FT still require their actual same-situation request owners, remaining work and budget.
+
+`GmSessionRunCoordinator.cs:126–130` creates a real OperationPin, enters Access and awaits the delegate inside the disposal scopes. Keeping a copied Access or child receipt cannot keep that root operation alive. `MainRunFence.cs:56–77,137–149,171–177,228–250` shows actual local/remote admission, retained borrowing and release; local CompleteAsync is a no-op while a remote close is a protocol action. The proposal correctly specifies a local-only original-parent sibling and denies remote/quiescent fallback, invented current G and new root authority from a data invocation.
+
+The new hook must precede actual binding closing, not use the existing closing hook: `SessionOperationContext.cs:121–155` retains an outer admission, calls RunBoundCore93–107 with its inner admission, then awaits RunBoundBody192–310. Nested bindings return through218–223; an outer binding starts main/state closing at257–258, before its read-only finalization lease at262–270. An existing caller-owned write lease follows a separate250–254 path. The proposal explicitly handles all these cases and places joins before closing. Captured semantic outcome is not a settlement hook. The actual parent body/pin must remain awaited until child, IO, storage and finalization obligations have genuine outcomes; failure or timeout cannot stand in for that exhaustion.
