+The promise-before-invocation and separate arm gate correctly distinguish registration, entered synchronous prefix, actual Task binding, native release and exact publication attempt. Seal winning before invocation can prove NeverInvoked; it cannot erase effects already entered. Arm winning admits only the frozen bounded attempt, not a successor computation, transaction retry, new member or semantic continuation. Runtime turn/response/snapshot mutations also require their own once-only effect boundary. The proposal does not infer original authority from metadata, IDs, paths, hashes or deserialization. Its parent/slot states and diagnostic schema remain proposed, not accepted persistent issuers.
