+The storage source justifies lower native attempt ownership. `FileSystemManager.TrustedLocalStorage.cs:181–252` creates directories at205 and mutation tracking at207 before publisher intent, invokes hooks/guards, and can retry a rolled-back transient attempt at236–246. `TrustedLocalFilePublication.cs:234–307` recovers before a new attempt, creates a new transaction ID at268, records Prepared at272 and then stages/publishes journal and members. Committed success can be returned despite cleanup failure (`TrustedLocalStorage:255–264`). Accordingly, no active journal, no thrown error, a successful facade return or the story child receipt is sufficient to establish zero debt.
